--- Finding (facial_detection_in_a_photo): `concat` of a list literal whose text interpolates a
--- value that can fail with a list of plain text does not build compiled.
---
--- Interpreted (crow run -i): prints
---     a crow b
--- Compiled (crow run):
---     error[E0308]: mismatched types
---     error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused what Crow
---     accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program (`crow run -i` runs it meanwhile)
--- Expected: "a crow b" in both modes.
--- The generated Rust: `let lines: Vec<CrowResult<String>> = crow_runtime::core::concat(
--- (vec![CrowResult { … format!("a {}", …) … }]), &(vec!["b".to_string()])[..])` — the
--- second list is not made a list of values that can fail (or the first's items decided).
--- Akin to findings/christofides_algorithm-2.co (concat of 64-bit ints with growing ints),
--- another pair of item kinds. Met writing an SVG: a header line naming a file whose name
--- came from a function that can fail, concatenated with the lines that draw the boxes.
fn named[t]
    if t eq ''
        return error['no name']
    return t

name = named['crow']
lines = concat[['a `name`'], ['b']]
log[join[lines, ' ']]
